# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Foretell Depart the Realm from hand, then cast it from exile on a later turn.
# Forcing: The scripted scenario must create the foretold state before the exile cast rail exists.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand and one vanilla permanent, so it has no protocol decisions.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the standalone Survive goal completed after the scripted path.
#   LOSE = turn progression or the bounce path failed before the deadline.
#   TIMEOUT = the Foretell action, later cast offer, targeting, or resolution stalled.
# Card roles:
#   Depart the Realm — Foretell lifecycle and targeted spell under test.
#   Grizzly Bears — deterministic nonland target for the foretold cast.
#   Islands — pay the {2} Foretell action and later {U} cast cost.
#   Basic lands in libraries — deterministic draw padding.
# Protocol path: Foretell hand-to-exile, face-down state, alternate cast, targeting, resolution, and cleanup.

[metadata]
Name:Foretell Depart the Realm
Goal:Survive
Turns:5
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Foretell Depart the Realm, then cast it from exile to return Grizzly Bears to its owner's hand.

[state]
ActivePlayer=Human
ActivePhase=Main1
HumanLife=20
AILife=20

humanhand=Depart the Realm
humanbattlefield=Island;Island
humanlibrary=Island;Island;Island
aibattlefield=Grizzly Bears
ailibrary=Forest;Forest;Forest
